<code>assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => !this.containsKey(key) && \result != null;</code>

This assert statement checks that if the key was previously in the map (`\old(this.containsKey(key))`), then after the removal operation, the key is no longer in the map (`!this.containsKey(key)`) and the value returned by the `remove` operation is not `null` (`\result != null`). Note that the condition `\result != null` is used to handle the case where the map might have explicitly mapped the key to `null`. If you want to strictly check that the value was present and not `null`, you might need additional context or a different approach. However, based on the given comment, this seems to be the most appropriate translation.
